{"name":"Judge Grey","hex":"#5d5346","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"judge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A public official whose duty it is to administer the law, especially by presiding over trials and rendering judgments; a justice.","A person who decides the fate of someone or something that has been called into question."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sit in judgment on; to pass sentence on (a person or matter).","To sit in judgment, to act as judge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judge"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Judge","blocks":[{"text":"A judge is a public official who presides over court proceedings, either alone or as a part of a judicial panel. In an adversarial system, the judge hears all the witnesses and any other evidence presented by the barristers or solicitors of the case, assesses the credibility and arguments of the parties, and then issues a ruling in the case based on their interpretation of the law and their own personal judgment. A judge is expected to conduct the trial impartially and, typically, in an open court."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/ICJ-CJI_hearing_1.jpg/330px-ICJ-CJI_hearing_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judge","wikidata":"Q16533"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg/500px-Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg/1280px-Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg/500px-Don_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"17th century Spanish judge in full gowns, by Velázquez","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADon_Diego_del_Corral_y_Arellano%2C_por_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/The_Native_Judges.jpg/500px-The_Native_Judges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/The_Native_Judges.jpg/500px-The_Native_Judges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"These drawings were taken from life in 1758. From left to right, top row: 1. Interpreter, Rhowangee Sewagee. 2. Judge of the Hindoo Law, Antoba Crustnagee Pundit. 3. Hindoo Officer, Lellather Chatta Bhutt. From left to right, bottom row: 4. Officer to the Mooremen, Mahmoud Ackram of the Codjee order or priesthood of the cast of Moormens. 5. Judge of the Mohomedan Law, Cajee Husson. 6. Haveldar, or summoning Officer, Mahmound Ismael'.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Native_Judges.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/President_Robert_Spano.jpg/500px-President_Robert_Spano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/President_Robert_Spano.jpg/500px-President_Robert_Spano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Róbert Ragnar Spanó, president of the European Court of Human Rights","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APresident_Robert_Spano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg/500px-Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg/1280px-Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg/500px-Supreme_Court_US_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The United States Supreme Court in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASupreme_Court_US_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cms_BANCOIMAGEMFOTOMINISTRO_bancoImagemFotoMinistro_AP_88800.jpg/500px-Cms_BANCOIMAGEMFOTOMINISTRO_bancoImagemFotoMinistro_AP_88800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cms_BANCOIMAGEMFOTOMINISTRO_bancoImagemFotoMinistro_AP_88800.jpg/1280px-Cms_BANCOIMAGEMFOTOMINISTRO_bancoImagemFotoMinistro_AP_88800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cms_BANCOIMAGEMFOTOMINISTRO_bancoImagemFotoMinistro_A